 # Ray Traversal and Integration Schemes
 
+
 ## Overview
-Ray Traversal and Integration Schemes define the aggregation logic applied to voxel samples collected along a ray to produce a final pixel value [S1, unofficial]. While [Ray Marching and Discretization](2788-ray-marching-and-discretization.md) determines where to sample, these schemes determine how to combine those samples . They are distinguished from standard front-to-back alpha compositing by their ability to perform non-compositional aggregations (such as Maximum or Average) or to simplify the compositing process for specific visualization goals like X-ray simulation [S1, unofficial].
